-- title:
--   Norm level transport: existence and uniqueness of Pₙ
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the Čerednik–Drinfeld package for fake elliptic curves, and its hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **The base ring.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adic completeness (`hcomplete`), $\#(\mathcal{O}/\pi) = r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **The unramified extension.** A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal{O}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, $\pi$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), with $\pi Onr$ maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`); thus $Onr/\pi Onr$ is an algebraically closed field of characteristic $r$ and $Fr$ induces the $r$-power Frobenius on it. Further, a monoid homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal{O}^\times$ (`hvdet`), i.e. the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **The indefinite quaternion algebra and its moduli.** Rationals $a, b$ with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ indefinite and a division algebra exactly at the primes containing $r$ or $\bar r$ (`hB`), and a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}$ with a point map `pt` which is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳`) for fake elliptic curves over $\mathcal{O}$-algebras: abelian schemes of relative fibre dimension $2$ with commutative relative group law, $\Lambda$-action satisfying the trace condition, and a level-$N$ subscheme.
--
--   **Full level $n$ and the twist action.** An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`); a fine moduli space $(M, fM, ptF)$ for pairs consisting of a fake elliptic curve and a full level-$n$ structure (`hM`); a group $G$ with $\rho : G \to \mathrm{Aut}(M)$ and labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ forming a level-twist action (`hρ`). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke correspondences and Atkin–Lehner maps on $\mathcal{X}$.** For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$, a scheme $\mathcal{Y}_\ell$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}$ with extra-level-$\ell$ point map $ptT$ which is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒴`), together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) computing, on points, forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and passing to a level-$\ell$ isogenous quotient (`hd₁`); endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); a finite idèle $n_1$ in the $r$-Hecke set of $R_1$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ containing $r$ (`hv`). The group $\Gamma_t$ is the group of units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all primes other than $v$ (`hΓt`); elements $s_\ell \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^\times$ and idèles $s_{f,\ell}$ are given for each $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, with `hs` requiring (four clauses) that $s_{f,\ell}$ agrees with $s_\ell$ at every prime not containing $r$, is $1$ at the primes containing $r$, that the diagonal idèle of the scalar $\ell$ times $s_{f,\ell}^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and that $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; and $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Coordinates on $\Lambda$.** All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and $coord : \Lambda \to W(\mathbb{F}_{r^2})^2$ is an order coordinatisation (`hcoord`): additive, unital, multiplicative in the $\varpi$-twisted sense, injective, with dense image modulo every power of $r$, and compatible with reduced traces.
--
--   **The special fibre.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/\pi Onr$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ over $Onr/\pi Onr$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0.f$ in two variables presenting $A_0$ via $coord$ and $X_0$ (`hA₀`), and families $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'` make $\Gamma_t$ act by $r$-power isogenies: each $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; $e$ is multiplicative up to multiplication by powers of $r$; rational-integer scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act by the corresponding scalar, and conversely only scalars act through the $\Lambda$-action by a positive integer. The hypothesis `hE2` states that for every injective ring homomorphism of the centraliser of $\{X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}\} \cup \{X_0.\varpi\mathrm{End}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ is realised on formal coordinates by a centraliser element $\varepsilon$ whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; `hE3` provides, for every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$, labels $lab : \Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ describing the action of $e\gamma$ on that structure, multiplicative modulo $n$ and sending scalars to scalars modulo $n$; `hE4` states that over any algebraically closed field over $Onr/\pi Onr$, any level-preserving $r$-power isogeny self-pair of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to $r$-power multiplications. The group `hE5a`–`hE5e` equips an order $R_2 \le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators in $R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) with endomorphisms $\hat e : R_2 \to \mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base (`hê`) which are additive on points, commute with the $\Lambda$-action and preserve the level (`hE5a`), are unital and multiplicative and send rational integers to the corresponding $\Lambda$-action (`hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`), satisfy $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = \mathrm{act}(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ (`hE5c`), agree with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$ up to $r$-power multiplications (`hE5d`), and admit a simultaneous matrix description for $\Gamma_t$ and for $R_2$ with a single $g$ (`hE5e`).
--
--   **The special formal module and its moduli package.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : W(\mathbb{F}_{r^2}) \to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/rOnr$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a map $\eta$ sending rigidified objects to points of $MD$, with `hη` requiring (three clauses) that $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, commutes with base change along ring maps over $Onr$, and is surjective after passage to a Zariski cover by admissible objects; an injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action endomorphisms and $\varpi$ of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal{O})$ through one fixed power $r^m$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   **The Drinfeld uniformisation of the package.** A family of maps $eD$ from the functor $\mathcal{G}_{\mathcal{O}}(MD)$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$, natural in the base (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), computing the first component as the leg $\psi$ (`hfstD`), transporting the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $\mathcal{G}_{\mathcal{O}}(MD)$ to the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), sending $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist of the first component (`hPiD`), with $\pi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Comparison of the two reductions.** A ring map $\kappa : Onr/\pi Onr \to Onr/rOnr$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner at $\bar r$ on the special fibre.** A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $Onr/\pi Onr$, morphisms $aw, aw'$ realising $A_0 \to A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`haw`, `haw'`, `hALw`), a pair $bw, bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{kw}$ from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ (`hbw`, `hBSw`) which preserves the level (`hBSwlev`), the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ lying over the base (`habw`), and `hJOINTw`, which strengthens `hE2` by producing one $g$ that simultaneously matches each $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $e\gamma$ and matches $\bar w$ with the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ on formal coordinates.
--
--   **The period map on rigidified curves.** A map $\Xi$ assigning to every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to B$ and every rigidified curve over $B$ with leg $\psi$ a point of $\mathcal{G}_{\mathcal{O}}(MD)(B)$, subject to: `hΞleg`, the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ when $B$ has no nontrivial idempotents; `hΞnat`, naturality under base change compatible with the rigidifications; `hΞiso`, invariance under an isomorphism of the underlying curves compatible with the reductions, the auxiliary pullbacks of $A_0$ and the rigidifying isogenies up to $r$-power multiplications; and `hΞdef`, which for connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent and a given formal-module presentation of the curve produces $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X$ the given formal module, a rig-transport relation relating $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ and the rigidification at level $j$, admissibility of $t$ for $\iota$ and the leg twisted by $Fr^{-j}$, and the identity $\Xi = \eta(t)$ with that twisted leg.
--
--   **The chosen matrix.** An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with two compatibility hypotheses: `heqΓ`, translation of a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, up to a power of the scalar matrix $r$, to the action of $g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ on the images under $\Xi$; and `heqW`, the analogous statement for an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (with $\bar r$ invertible in $B$) and the element $\bar w$, under the stated comparison of the two rigidifications through the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The assertion is the conjunction of two statements, both quantified over all Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, all $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps $\psi : Onr \to B$, all fake elliptic curves $E$ over $B$ and all rigidifications $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ with leg the Frobenius twist $\psi \circ Fr^{-v(\det g_0)}$, where $v(\det g_0)$ denotes the integer underlying $vdet(g_0)$.
--
--   First (existence): if in addition every idempotent of $B$ is $0$ or $1$, and a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ over $B$ together with formal coordinates $\theta$ of $E.f$ in two variables present $E$ via $coord$, then there exists a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ which is a norm level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$, that is: there is a morphism $Q : \mathrm{Spec}(B/\pi B) \to \varrho.A_b$ which is a section of the structure morphism of $\varrho.A_b$, whose composite with $\varrho.g_A$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the residue map $Onr/\pi Onr \to B/\pi B$ followed by the section $P_0.P$; and there exist a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X'$ over $B$, formal coordinates $\theta'$ presenting $E$ via $coord$, an integer $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ for $\Phi$ over $B$ with $t.X = X'$, such that $\theta'$, $j$ and $t$ form a rig-transport of $\theta_0$ along $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ for $\varrho$, $t$ is admissible for $\iota$ and the leg $\psi' \circ Fr^{-j}$ of $\varrho$, and the reduction modulo $\pi$ of the $r^{t.n}$-fold multiple of $P_n.P$ for the group law of $E$ equals $Q$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi'$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$.
--
--   Second (uniqueness): for all full level-$n$ structures $P_n$ and $P_n'$ on $E$, if each is a norm level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$ in the above sense, then the underlying sections coincide, $P_n.P = P_n'.P$. This second assertion is stated without the connectedness hypothesis on $B$ and without any given formal-module presentation of $E$.
--
--   This is the level-structure step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison for fake elliptic curves: it transports the fixed full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on the special-fibre curve $A_0$ to any rigidified curve over a Noetherian base in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, and shows the transported structure is determined by its defining compatibility. It is used downstream in the construction of presentation labels for $\Gamma_t$ and in the identification of rigidified points of the moduli package with points of the Drinfeld space carrying level structure.
